<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="9141c036">&lt;p&gt;
    Prepare the package application for release with the complete set of development objects,&amp;nbsp;such as reports,
    interfaces, conversions, extensions, forms, workflows, and security components. The set of development objects to be
    released is usually&amp;nbsp;governed by&amp;nbsp;the software development plan. Most importantly, the set of objects to be
    released have no known defects and can be sent for system testing.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    The application build may involve vendor-specific application build tools, assemblers, or other organization scripts
    which takes a set of development objects&amp;nbsp;and bundles them together.&amp;nbsp;Application builds could also involve
    the&amp;nbsp;authoring and creation of installers for use by test teams or by end-users.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The specific way to package an application will largely depends on the application being built but in general the steps
    should be:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    1. Organize&amp;nbsp;the set of unit-tested development objects:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    2. Remove any debugging settings
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    3. Build or package the application components using the vendor-specific tool
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    4. Identify any data sets to be used and notify the data migration team 5. Submit the application build to migration
    team to move the development objects from the development environment to the testing environment. This task can be
    performed along with other transports either manually or by batch job. In the testing environment the custom code will
    be tested along with other test items to make sure desired results are achieved without breaking other business
    processes or the technical integrity of the system.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    5. Submit the application build to migration team to move the development objects from the development environment to
    the testing environment. This task can be performed along with other transports either manually or by batch job. In the
    testing environment, the custom code will be tested along with other test items to make sure desired results are
    achieved without breaking other business processes or the technical integrity of the system.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    6. Create an installation guide, including the overall installation plan, configuration documents, functional and
    technical documentation), that will walk the implementation team through the specific steps required to install the
    system.&lt;br /&gt;
    Create the guide by:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conducting an installation planning session to identify the requirements: infrastructure, software, database,
        software and database versions, patches, system admin or other users, system administrator rights, connections to
        other systems/tools/databases/applications
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Defining the system landscape, system variants, number of instances
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identifying any relevant system administration users, connectivity requirements to other tools, applications,
        systems or databases&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
